## Apollo Client — Kya Hai Aur Kab Use Karo

Apollo Client GraphQL ke liye ek **dedicated library** hai — TanStack Query + fetch dono ko replace karta hai.

```
Apollo Client kya karta hai:
  ✓ GraphQL queries/mutations manage karta hai
  ✓ In-memory cache (TanStack Query jaisa)
  ✓ Auto refetch
  ✓ Optimistic updates
  ✓ Real-time subscriptions (WebSocket)

TanStack Query kya karta hai:
  ✓ Kisi bhi async function ka cache manage karta hai
  ✓ REST, GraphQL, ya kuch bhi
  ✗ GraphQL-specific features nahi (subscriptions, fragments)
```

```javascript
// Apollo Client setup
import { ApolloClient, InMemoryCache, gql, useQuery } from '@apollo/client';

const client = new ApolloClient({
  uri: 'https://api.linear.app/graphql',
  cache: new InMemoryCache(),
  headers: {
    Authorization: process.env.LINEAR_API_KEY
  }
});

// Apollo ka useQuery — automatic caching aur loading states
const GET_MY_ISSUES = gql`
  query GetMyIssues {
    viewer {
      assignedIssues {
        nodes {
          id
          title
          priority
        }
      }
    }
  }
`;

function IssueList() {
  const { loading, error, data } = useQuery(GET_MY_ISSUES);

  if (loading) return <p>Loading...</p>;
  if (error) return <p>Error: {error.message}</p>;

  return (
    <ul>
      {data.viewer.assignedIssues.nodes.map(issue => (
        <li key={issue.id}>{issue.title}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

```
Apollo use karo jab:
  → Pure GraphQL project ho
  → Real-time subscriptions chahiye ho
  → Large team, GraphQL-first approach

TanStack Query use karo jab:
  → Mix of REST + GraphQL ho
  → Already REST APIs bhi hain project mein
  → Simple setup chahiye
```

