## Flow Summary — Ek Line Mein Har Concept

```
GraphQL    = Ek endpoint pe apni marzi ka data maango
Query      = Data padhna (GET)
Mutation   = Data banana/badalna/hatana (POST/PUT/DELETE)
Pagination = Cursor se page by page data lena
Schema     = Poori API ki definition — kya available hai
Resolver   = Behind the scenes jo actually data laata hai
Apollo     = GraphQL ke liye dedicated React library
TanStack   = Kisi bhi async ke liye cache library
Linear SDK = Linear GraphQL ko wrap karta hai — queries likhni nahi padti
Postman    = Still useful, but GraphQL mode mein ya Altair use karo
Versioning = URL nahi badlata, fields add/deprecate hote hain

REST se fark:
  REST  → Multiple URLs, fixed response, versioned endpoints
  GraphQL → Ek URL, flexible response, schema evolves gracefully
```

